nes and Joints — 20-Mark University Exam Answers Page 1 of 23◦ ◦ Cellulitis Chronic wound Predisposing factors • • • •\n<truncated 22224 bytes>\nl evaluation If Charcot arthropathy is suspected: • • • • Sensory examination Proprioception Reflexes Neurological assessment Differential Diagnosis • • • • • • Rheumatoid arthritis Osteoarthritis Septic arthritis Tuberculous arthritis Gout Neuropathic arthropathy due to other causes Complications • • • • • • • • • Joint destruction Deformity Subluxation Dislocation Pathological fracture Instability Loss of function Secondary osteoarthritis Neurological disability in associated neurosyphilis Page 21 of 23 Diseases of Bones and Joints — 20-Mark University Exam AnswersMedical Management Specific treatment Penicillin-based therapy is the standard treatment for syphilis, with the exact preparation, dose and duration determined by the stage and clinical form of disease. Management may include: • • • • • • Appropriate penicillin therapy Treatment of sexual partners according to public-health guidance Screening for other sexually transmitted infections Neurological evaluation when indicated Analgesics Management of secondary complications For Charcot arthropathy • • • • • Protection from excessive loading Off-loading Appropriate orthosis Footwear modification where applicable Management of associated neurological disease Surgical Management Surgery is generally directed toward the resulting structural damage rather than eradication of the infection itself. May include: • • • • • • Synovectomy in selected cases Debridement when indicated Arthrodesis for severe instability Joint reconstruction Joint replacement in selected patients after appropriate infection treatment Correction of severe deformity Rehabilitation • • • • • • • • Protection of affected joint Pain management Maintaining safe ROM Muscle strengthening Orthotic support Gait training Assistive devices when required Patient education regarding joint protection\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-13T16:36:44+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
