 orthoses reconstructive surgery and self care education help prevent disability and maintain function","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm focusing on the most efficient tool utilization. It's becoming clearer that prioritizing specific tools will drastically improve my problem-solving ability. The goal is to always select the tool best suited for the immediate task at hand, regardless of how broad a command may be. This will keep work on the project organized.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Selection**\n\nI'm now prioritizing precise tool selection based on new guidelines. Remembering instruction 1, I am avoiding `cat`, internal `grep`, `ls`, and others for certain tasks. Regarding instruction 2, I'm analyzing the tools needed to remove page numbers embedded in the text. I've identified the use of `sed` as a likely tool and am considering if any other tools will be needed to handle this task.\n\n\n**Defining Cerebral Palsy**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on defining Cerebral Palsy for this project. The focus is on the permanent nature of the movement and posture disorders the limitations they cause and that the cause is a non progressive disturbance during development. It's crucial to acknowledge the possibility of co-occurring sensory perceptual cognitive communication behavioral and epileptic disturbances.\n\n\n**Analyzing CP Factors**\n\nI'm now delving into the causes and classification of Cerebral Palsy. Identifying prenatal, perinatal, and postnatal risk factors is key. Differentiating spastic, dyskinetic, ataxic, and mixed CP types is the next step. I'm also analyzing clinical features and associated complications to gain a broader understanding of the condition.\n\n\n**Outlining Treatments & Assessments**\n\nI'm now outlining treatments and assessment methods for Cerebral Palsy, considering diverse approaches. I'm focusing on the necessity of comprehensive neurological and developmental assessments, as well as imaging techniques such as MRI and EEG. Medical manag